    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever read "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "music",
            "zh": "识谱"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? You may see the word “presto” at the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "beginning",
            "ref": "v-beginning"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of a song. Or you may find “piano” and “fortissimo” in the middle. These words are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Italian",
            "ref": "v-italian"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "! It’s called the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "language",
            "ref": "v-language"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that sings."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Thousands of years ago, people could only pass songs down "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "orally",
            "zh": "口头地"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Ancient",
            "ref": "v-ancient"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Babylonia",
            "zh": "巴比伦"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Greece",
            "zh": "希腊"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Rome",
            "zh": "罗马"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " were some of the earliest to write music. Later, people in Spain and Italy began putting music to paper."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Around 1000 AD, an Italian man named Guido d’Arezzo* came up with the musical "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "stave",
            "zh": "五线谱"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This is used to show "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pitch",
            "zh": "音高"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in written music. Over the next few centuries, a lot of people used Italian words to write music."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "musical vocabulary",
            "zh": "音乐词汇"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is full of Italian words. Let’s see some examples!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The word “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "adagio",
            "zh": "慢板"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” tells players the music should be slow; “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "allegro",
            "zh": "快板"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” or “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "presto",
            "zh": "急板"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” tells them to play fast or very fast; “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "piano",
            "zh": "轻柔"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” or “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "fortissimo",
            "zh": "极强"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” tells them to play quietly or very loudly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Players should stop playing when they see “Fine”. It means the “end”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*吉多·达雷佐（Guido d’Arezzo），意大利中世纪音乐理论家，五线谱的发明者。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
